  (no_connect (at 99.06 96.52) (uuid 7b87abc1-7c8d-5875-90c8-099dd4146a63))
  (no_connect (at 193.04 146.05) (uuid 288fc464-6246-5e6e-871c-2a4a89eae58d))
  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nA LONE NO-CONNECT PIN'S NET IS NAMED AFTER THE PIN (the export names it so, whatever label it carries), so the\none-pin nets the text below names are, on this sheet: SPARE_GATE_OUT is 4Y; CS_PULLUP_TOP is 2.\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in digital-and-supervision.md is a REPRESENTATION of this\nfile.\n\nALL SIX R-SPI-PULL INSTANCES ARE PLACED HERE. The row lives in interfaces/spi-link's bom.csv because that page\nderives the values, but the resistors are on the module board on both sides of this buffer, and the drawing\nabove shows both triples. Owning a row and placing an instance are different things; `of:` is what says so.\n\nONE OF THE SIX HAS NOWHERE TO GO - see CS_PULLUP_TOP at the bottom.\n\n[pins] WHICH SIGNAL GETS WHICH GATE IS ASSIGNED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE [derived, not cited]. No page states it;\na netlist has to. Gate 4 is the spare the BOM row mentions. Contradict this in the page and the file follows.\n\n--- cable side: the three pulls that hold the BUFFER's inputs ------\n\n--- DAC side: the three that hold the DAC's inputs ----------------\n\nThese were bought for the state the cable-side three do not reach: module alive, instrument off, which is\nNORMAL and not a fault.\n\n[DIG_GND] THE FOUR ENABLES ARE TIED, NOT DRIVEN. OE_MOD is in hardware/nets.yaml's `retired:` section for\nexactly this reason: the comparator that gated it is not fitted, so there is no net crossing a boundary - just\nfour pins on the local ground.\n\n[4Y] THE SPARE GATE'S INPUT IS TIED, and it is tied because the BOM row says \"TIE EVERY UNUSED INPUT TO VCC OR\nGND\" - a floating CMOS input on an enabled gate is the one wrong answer. GND is chosen over VCC because the\npart has no input clamp to VCC and the ground tie cannot inject current into an unpowered rail. Its output\ndrives nothing, which is fine.\n\n*** THE CABLE-SIDE CS PULL-UP HAS NO RAIL ON THIS BOARD. ***\n\nR-SPI-PULL's own row says \"CABLE-SIDE CS PULLS TO 3V3, NOT +5V\", with the reason: at 5 V it drives 430 uA\ncontinuously through the unpowered ESP32's input clamp in the design's normal resting state, and the node sits\nat ~0.7 V so \"CS idle high\" is not achieved at all. The reasoning is sound and the rail does not exist here -\nthe umbilical carries BREATH/AGND, +12V/PWR_GND, SCLK/MOSI and CS/DIG_GND, and the module makes +12, -12, bus\n+5 and DAC AVDD. There is no 3V3 anywhere on this board.\n\n['2'] So either this resistor belongs at the INSTRUMENT end, where 3V3 exists and where its own argument about\nthe ESP32's clamp is measured, or the row's \"at the module\" description is right and the rail has to come from\nsomewhere. Both cannot be true. Nothing is asserted until it is decided; digital-and-supervision.md's \"Still\nopen\" carries the question." (at 256.54 38.099999999999994 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid cd626b92-20f2-58b8-b2aa-b31952beacda))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
